msgid "GB123_GSOR_1006_v7_Halloween_event"
msgstr "Havoc"

msgid "GB123_GSOR_1006_v7_Halloween_event_descr"
msgstr ""
"The machine codenamed Havoc was first tested during the expedition to the "
"Dark Tower. The combination of a wheeled chassis, a rapid-fire cannon with a"
" magazine-fed loading system, and Mirium enhancements proved highly "
"effective in the deeper phases of the Anomaly, with their unpredictable "
"effects. Tank crews noted the model's flexibility and broad functionality."

msgid "GB123_GSOR_1006_v7_Halloween_event_long_special"
msgstr ""
"A versatile vehicle that combines a wheeled chassis and a rapid-fire "
"automatic cannon."

msgid "GB123_GSOR_1006_v7_Halloween_event_short"
msgstr "Havoc"

msgid "GB125_Saladin_HW_BOT"
msgstr "Detonator"

msgid "GB125_Saladin_HW_BOT_descr"
msgstr ""
"The FV601 Saladin wheeled armored vehicle, designed by Alvis Car and "
"Engineering Company, was meant to replace the AEC Armoured Car. Work started"
" in 1946, but the practical stage did not begin until the first half of the "
"1950s. The vehicle's distinctive features were its chassis with 6x6 wheel "
"configuration and its outrigger suspension. The first two prototypes of the "
"FV 601 (B) were produced in 1955. Two years later, a total of six pilot "
"armored vehicles were built, and in 1958, mass production was launched. The "
"armored vehicle was produced until 1972, most often in the Saladin Mk. 2 "
"modification. A total of 1,177 vehicles were built. The vehicle was actively"
" used in the Middle East and Africa."

msgid "GB125_Saladin_HW_BOT_short"
msgstr "Detonator"

msgid "GB24_Centurion_Mk3_HW_BOT"
msgstr "Corrupted Cerberus"

msgid "GB24_Centurion_Mk3_HW_BOT_descr"
msgstr ""
"A medium tank with mediocre mobility, reliable frontal armor, and an "
"excellent gun."

msgid "GB24_Centurion_Mk3_HW_BOT_short"
msgstr "Corrupted"

msgid "GB24_Centurion_Mk3_Halloween_event"
msgstr "Cerberus"

msgid "GB24_Centurion_Mk3_Halloween_event_descr"
msgstr ""
"With the British Centurion Mk.3 serving as its base, the development of the "
"Cerberus was driven by the need for a versatile medium tank capable of "
"operating in hostile environmental conditions. The resulting combination of "
"excellent armor, powerful weaponry, and Mirium-based enhancements proved so "
"effective that Cerberus tanks became all but mandatory for operations "
"conducted within the anomaly."

msgid "GB24_Centurion_Mk3_Halloween_event_long_special"
msgstr ""
"A medium tank with mediocre mobility, reliable frontal armor, and an "
"excellent gun."

msgid "GB24_Centurion_Mk3_Halloween_event_short"
msgstr "Cerberus"

